Title: 0017-coalesce-window-size-events
Repository: pragtical
Base-Commit: 5c05f09e081833b581fb5ecd10e64963dec87f03
Requires: 0016-dirmonitor-stop-threads-at-exit.patch
Author: aros-pragtical project
Date: 2026-11-18
Upstream-Status: candidate
Scope: src/system_events.c; all platforms.

Problem:
  A window resized continuously queues many size events between two frames; each one makes the renderer fetch a new window surface and redraw, which loads the system and allocates a new framebuffer per event.
Solution:
  When a size event for a window is already queued, replace its size with the newer one instead of queueing another, as is done for mouse motion.
Validation:
  not-run
Removal:
  Fill in when this is a workaround; permanent fixes say so here.

diff --git a/src/system_events.c b/src/system_events.c
index 45c770aa..c1738923 100644
--- a/src/system_events.c
+++ b/src/system_events.c
@@ -87,6 +87,22 @@ void system_push_event(const SDL_Event *event) {
   if (!system_event_is_handled(event->type))
     return;
 
+  /* Keep only the newest size of a window: every queued size event makes the
+   * renderer fetch a new window surface and redraw, and a window resized
+   * continuously sends many of them between two frames. */
+  if (event->type == SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_RESIZED ||
+      event->type == SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_PIXEL_SIZE_CHANGED) {
+    for (int i = system_event_queue_count - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
+      int idx = (system_event_queue_read + i) % SYSTEM_EVENT_QUEUE_SIZE;
+      if (system_event_queue[idx].type == event->type &&
+          system_event_queue[idx].window.windowID == event->window.windowID) {
+        system_event_queue[idx].window.data1 = event->window.data1;
+        system_event_queue[idx].window.data2 = event->window.data2;
+        return;
+      }
+    }
+  }
+
   /* Coalesce consecutive mouse-motion events for the same window */
   if (event->type == SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_MOTION) {
     for (int i = system_event_queue_count - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
